1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:04,460
- Well, I actually might be able to help.
- How so?

2
00:00:04,629 --> 00:00:07,129
(Sheldon:)Like Jane Goodall observing the apes...

3
00:00:07,299 --> 00:00:11,009
(Sheldon:)...I initially saw their interactions
as confusing and unstructured.

4
00:00:11,177 --> 00:00:12,217
(Sheldon:)But patterns emerge.

5
00:00:12,387 --> 00:00:15,807
(Sheldon:)They have their own language,
if you will.

6
00:00:16,725 --> 00:00:18,145
(Leonard:)Go on.

7
00:00:18,310 --> 00:00:21,650
(Sheldon:)Well, it seems that the newcomer
approaches the existing group...

8
00:00:21,813 --> 00:00:24,353
(Sheldon:)...with the greeting,
"How wasted am I?"

9
00:00:24,524 --> 00:00:28,324
(Sheldon:)Which is met
with an approving chorus of "Dude."

10
00:00:29,029 --> 00:00:30,199
(Leonard:)Then what happens?

11
00:00:30,363 --> 00:00:32,033
(Sheldon:)That's as far as I've gotten.

12
00:00:33,491 --> 00:00:34,821
(Leonard:)This is ridiculous.

13
00:00:34,993 --> 00:00:36,993
(Leonard:)- I'm jumping in.
- Good luck.

14
00:00:37,162 --> 00:00:38,542
(Leonard:)No, you're coming with me.

15
00:00:38,705 --> 00:00:40,705
(Sheldon:)Oh, I hardly think so.

16
00:00:40,874 --> 00:00:41,914
(Leonard:)Come on.

17
00:00:42,542 --> 00:00:46,712
- Aren't you afraid I'll embarrass you?
- Yes, but I need a wingman.

18
00:00:46,880 --> 00:00:49,670
All right, but if we're going
to use flight metaphors...

19
00:00:49,841 --> 00:00:54,511
(Sheldon:)...I'm much more suited to being the guy
from the FAA analyzing wreckage.

20
00:00:56,640 --> 00:00:58,020
(Girl in Hippie Costume:)Oh, hi.

